# Security

## 1. Webview Sandbox

- The webview MUST run with the minimum required privileges:
  - `enableScripts: true` ONLY if the UI needs it; `enableCommandUris` MUST remain
    `false`.
  - `localResourceRoots` MUST be restricted to the extension's own `media/` and
    `webview/` folders — never the whole workspace or machine.
- MUST NOT load remote content (no external scripts, styles, images, or iframes).
- MUST NOT use `retainContextWhenHidden` unless required; prefer releasing webview
  resources when hidden.

## 2. Content Security Policy

- The webview `index.html` MUST include a strict `Content-Security-Policy` `meta` tag:
  `default-src 'none'; script-src 'nonce-<id>'; style-src 'nonce-<id>'; img-src ...` —
  allowing only the extension's local resources.

## 3. Untrusted Input & Output

- Markdown file contents and note titles are UNTRUSTED. Treat them as data, not markup.
- NEVER inject note titles or content into the webview via `innerHTML`. Use `textContent`
  or canvas text drawing (`ctx.fillText`), which cannot execute HTML/JS.
- Sanitize or escape any value before it reaches `postMessage` or the DOM.

## 4. Secrets & Configuration

- API keys, tokens, and credentials MUST live in VS Code configuration or environment
  variables. They MUST NEVER be hardcoded in source.
- Secrets MUST NEVER be committed to version control. Add them to `.gitignore`.

## 5. Error Handling & Visibility

- Fail fast and loud. A failed operation MUST surface an error; it MUST NOT be silently
  ignored.
- File operations MUST be bounded to the workspace and read-only unless the feature
  explicitly writes (which v1 does not).

## Examples

### Correct — restricted webview with nonce

```ts
const panel = vscode.window.createWebviewPanel(
  "atlas",
  "Graph",
  vscode.ViewColumn.One,
  {
    enableScripts: true,
    enableCommandUris: false,
    localResourceRoots: [vscode.Uri.joinPath(extensionUri, "media")],
  }
);
```

```html
<meta
  http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
  content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'nonce-abc'; style-src 'nonce-abc';"
/>
```

### Incorrect — NEVER do these

```ts
// Bad: unrestricted webview
localResourceRoots: [vscode.Uri.file("C:/")];
```

```ts
// Bad: injecting untrusted note title as HTML
nodeEl.innerHTML = note.title;
```

```ts
const apiKey = "sk-..."; // hardcoded secret
```
